Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:54:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] phase2-audit: one home for the 40 cm body radius + the
 contact ring (B-1, B-5)

The body radius was typed by hand in three places, two of which bypassed
the values the seam already carries:
- EngagementClustersProcessor dilated OBBs with local constexpr 0.4f/0.7f
  while the seam's FAssignContext (DefenderRadiusM/AttackerRadiusM +
  ReachByClassM) defines the same numbers the pairing ring uses -- a cvar
  edit to the context would silently desync contact detection from pairing
- AssignPairsProcessor's write-back re-derived the ring as '0.4f + 0.4f +
  reach', ignoring the seam's RingRadiusFor helper used one screen earlier
- ServoProcessor re-typed 0.4f at three avoidance/touch sites

Fix:
- FCombatSolver::Contact::BodyRadiusM named constant in BattleEngagement.h
- RingRadiusFor(uint8 ReachClass, const FAssignContext&) promoted from the
  anonymous namespace to the public seam API (same formula, same clamps)
- all consumers (cluster dilation, assign ring, servo radii) now read the
  same source; the cluster dilation reads the reach table's Normal entry
  instead of a re-typed 0.7f
- FMeleeMathConstants::MinChargeRunUpM names the charge run-up gate that
  ChargeProcessor compared against the literal 1.f

Same values everywhere (0.4/0.7 preserved); one source. T2.1 golden must
be re-run on the UE machine as a formality (no seam signature it pins
changed shape).
